    the domain. If the question is strictly about what HTTPS protects, the answer is
    yes. The tempting answer is "no" because people point to SNI and DNS leakage, but
    that confuses transport metadata with the encrypted HTTP exchange. HTTPS does hide
    the domain from the HTTP conversation.
